kr3=[0,cp,[0,g,bbJ]],kr4=eQ,kr5=[0,cd,[0,g,eQ]],kr6="\nRemoves **only** the statics refractor from the bindings at the given paths.\nRuntime probes on the same binding are left unchanged (unlike remove_probe).\n\nParameters:\npaths: list(string) \xe2\x80\x94 paths to the bindings to clear statics overlays from\n",kr7=[0,[0,lb,[0,V,[0,[0,cd,[0,g,jz]],[0,[0,kl,[0,V,[0,[0,lo,[0,V,[0,pve,pvd]]],0]]],[0,[0,hT,[0,h,[0,[0,g,lo],0]]],0]]]]],0],kr8=dV,kr9=[0,cp,[0,g,bh2]],kr_=eQ,kr$=[0,cd,[0,g,eQ]],ksa="\nToggles the statics refractor on or off for the bindings at the given paths (same behavior as the editor statics toggle).\nCollapsed definitions are auto-expanded when statics end up enabled.\n\nParameters:\npaths: list(string) \xe2\x80\x94 paths to the bindings to toggle\n",ksb=[0,[0,lb,[0,V,[0,[0,cd,[0,g,jz]],[0,[0,kl,[0,V,[0,[0,lo,[0,V,[0,pvg,pvf]]],0]]],[0,[0,hT,[0,h,[0,[0,g,lo],0]]],0]]]]],0],ksc=dV,ksd=[0,cp,[0,g,bea]],kse=eQ,ksf=[0,cd,[0,g,eQ]],ksg=[0,0,0],ksq=[0,1],ksp=F,kso=F,ksn=F,ksm=m,ksl=co,ksk="Printer.add_indent: Not_found",ksr=[0,m],kss=[0,iy],ksu=[0,"- **checkbox** \xe2\x80\x94 Toggle UI for boolean literals."],ksv=[0,"- **slider** \xe2\x80\x94 Numeric literal editor (integer)."],ksw=[0,"- **sliderf** \xe2\x80\x94 Numeric literal editor (floating-point)."],ksx=[0,"- **card** \xe2\x80\x94 **Playing-card** editor: a tuple `(Suit, Rank)` such as `(Hearts, Ace)` or a list of those tuples. **Not** for records, modules, or `{ let \xe2\x80\xa6; \xe2\x80\xa6 }` blocks."],ksy=[0,"- **livelit** \xe2\x80\x94 Custom livelit projector for structured literal editing."],ksz=[0,"- **text** \xe2\x80\x94 Multiline string literal editor."],ksA=[0,"- **table** \xe2\x80\x94 Spreadsheet-style editor for a **list of labeled tuples** sharing the same labels; the labels become column headers. Attaches off the **elaborated** form, so it can apply where the surface syntax alone is not yet a table."],ksB=[0,"- **csv** \xe2\x80\x94 CSV **file import** UI. Attaches only when the definition is the **empty list** `[]`; after placement, import fills it with row/tuple syntax. Non-empty lists (e.g. `[1, 2, 3]`) **cannot** take this projector."],ksC=[0,0,0],ksD=[0,m,[0,"These are alternative UIs for literals and structured values that may already appear in code.",0]],ksE=[0,"### Livelits (menu projectors)",0],ksG=[0,m,0],ksH=[0,m,[0,"### Syntax projector tools (Filbert)",[0,"`place_syntax_projector(kind, paths)`, `remove_syntax_projector(paths)`, and `toggle_syntax_projector(kind, paths)` apply **syntax projector** UIs to the term selected by each path.",[0,"`kind` must be a menu projector name (`fold`, `slider`, `sliderf`, `check`, `text`, `card`, `csv`, `table`, `livelit`) \xe2\x80\x94 not `probe` or `statics` (those use the probe/statics tools).",[0,m,[0,"**CRITICAL \xe2\x80\x94 livelits are not automatic:** Ordinary Hazel code (`let speed = 50`, `let is_active = true`, list literals, records) renders as **plain text** until you call **`place_syntax_projector`**.",[0,'If the user asks how livelits work, or wants sliders/checkboxes/CSV editors/text boxes, you **must** call `place_syntax_projector` with the right `kind` on each binding path (e.g. `slider` on `"speed"`, `check` on `"is_active"`, `text` on `"message"`, `csv` only when the RHS is `[]`, `card` only on playing-card tuples/lists\xe2\x80\x94see livelit lines above; nested paths like `"config/volume"`).',[0,"**Never** describe interactive widgets as present based only on `insert_*`, `update_*`, or other edit tools \xe2\x80\x94 that is false unless the matching `place_syntax_projector` calls succeeded.",[0,m,0]]]]]]]]],ksI=kY(["## Projectors and the agent view",m,"### Fold (`\xe2\x8b\xb1`)","A **fold** is a collapsed definition in the GUI: the definition shows as `\xe2\x8b\xb1` (not source text).","Use `expand` / `collapse` (see **Paths** and **View Tools** above).",m,"### Runtime probe refractor","The **probe** refractor attaches to a binding and shows evaluated values in the agent view (e.g. `expr \xe2\x89\xa1 value`).","Tools: `place_probe`, `remove_probe`, `toggle_probe`.",m,"### Statics refractor (type overlay)","The **statics** refractor shows a type ascription overlay in the GUI (offside type cell) for human clarity.","It does not change program text; the agent\xe2\x80\x99s printed context may not mirror the overlay unless printing is extended.",m]),ksK=[0,"**Projectors**: **Folds** display as `\xe2\x8b\xb1` (collapsed defs; expand/collapse in the full prompt).",[0,"**Refractors** overlay bindings: **probes** show runtime values (`\xe2\x89\xa1` in context); **statics** add a type overlay in the GUI.",[0,"**Livelits** are alternate UIs for literals (checkbox, slider/sliderf, text, card, csv, table, livelit, plus fold in the menu).",[0,"**Agent tools**: `place_syntax_projector` / `remove_syntax_projector` / `toggle_syntax_projector` (see full prompt).",[0,"Full detail lives in Filbert\xe2\x80\x99s live system prompt **Projectors and the agent view** section (this excerpt may be truncated).",0]]]]],ksP="Editor.Meta.t_of_yojson",ksO="Editor.Meta.yojson_of_t",ksN="Editor.Meta.t_of_sexp",ksL="Editor.Meta.sexp_of_t",ksW=[0,0,[0,1,[0,2,[0,3,0]]]],ksV=[0,0,[0,1,[0,2,[0,3,0]]]],ksX=[0,0,[0,1,[0,2,[0,3,0]]]],ksU=[0,"Empty hole"],ksT=gP,ksS=[0,"Missing operator"],ksQ=[0,0,1],ksR=[0,0,0],ksY=[0,[0,lb,[0,V,[0,[0,cd,[0,g,jz]],[0,[0,kl,[0,V,[0,[0,lo,[0,V,[0,pvi,pvh]]],0]]],[0,[0,hT,[0,h,[0,[0,g,lo],0]]],0]]]]],0],ksZ=dV,ks0=[0,cp,[0,g,bhm]],ks1=eQ,ks2=[0,cd,[0,g,eQ]],ks3=[0,[0,lb,[0,V,[0,[0,cd,[0,g,jz]],[0,[0,kl,[0,V,[0,[0,lo,[0,V,[0,pvk,pvj]]],0]]],[0,[0,hT,[0,h,[0,[0,g,lo],0]]],0]]]]],0],ks4=dV,ks5=[0,cp,[0,g,beE]],ks6=eQ,ks7=[0,cd,[0,g,eQ]],ks8=[0,[0,lb,[0,V,[0,[0,cd,[0,g,jz]],[0,[0,kl,[0,V,[0,[0,lo,[0,V,[0,pvm,pvl]]],0]]],[0,[0,hT,[0,h,[0,[0,g,lo],0]]],0]]]]],0],ks9=dV,ks_=[0,cp,[0,g,bcY]],ks$=eQ,kta=[0,cd,[0,g,eQ]],ktq=[0,1],ktn=[0,Lx],kto=[0,F],ktp=co,ktl=[0,40],ktk=[0,kW],ktm=m,ktj=[0,0],kte=[0,1],ktf=[0,m],ktg=[0,iy],kth=F,kti=co,ktb=bV_,ktc=dsG,ktd=bS3,kt